From: h0cheung <hcheunh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: avoid synchronous MHI wake during Elden panic

Extend the existing panic-context MHI wake guard to Elden's wifi7 PCI
path. A failed wake also skips its matching release. Do not enable the
periodic RX refill watchdog or alter normal scan/RX handling.

Link: https://github.com/mydanyi/armadaos-freedom/tree/244b74516d99d06cb0518609ce4b842ab278be8a
Link: https://github.com/mydanyi/armadaos-freedom/blob/244b74516d99d06cb0518609ce4b842ab278be8a/packages/kernel/patches/0194-wifi-ath12k-baldur-rx-panic.patch
Signed-off-by: h0cheung <hcheunh@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/pci.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/pci.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/pci.c
@@ -72,7 +72,8 @@
 	 * return also skips the matching release.
 	 */
 	if (panic_in_progress() &&
-	    of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,baldur"))
+	    (of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,baldur") ||
+	     of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,elden")))
 		return -EBUSY;
 
 	return mhi_device_get_sync(ab_pci->mhi_ctrl->mhi_dev);
